  (text_box "Description: Human-Machine Interface (HMI)\nRotary encoders (×6): Bourns PEC11R incremental (quadrature) encoders with push switches form the front-panel controls - VPOSITION, VSCALE, HPOSITION, HSCALE, TRIG, and display. Each provides A/B quadrature outputs (rotation + direction) and a momentary push switch. All lines are RC-filtered: A/B use a lighter filter (10 kΩ + 10 nF) to preserve fast rotation pulses, while each switch uses a split RC (1 kΩ / 9 kΩ + 100 nF) for firm debouncing. Encoder commons tie to GND; A/B are read via the STM32 (timer encoder mode or GPIO interrupts) and the switches as GPIO inputs.\nDisplay (J8): Waveshare 16498 2.4\" IPS LCD (ILI9341, 320×240) on an SPI interface (SPI2: SCK/MISO/MOSI/NSS) plus RESET, DC/CNT, IRQ, and backlight control. Display logic powered from +5 V; SPI/control lines at +3V3 logic level."
    (at 177.8 139.7 0) (size 104.14 22.86)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) (thickness 0.254) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid 16124f04-42f6-4bbf-9747-512cab99ec4d)
  )

